---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Open Replicant">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__content">
      <span class="badge badge--open-source">Open Source AI · Apache-2.0</span>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="hero__tagline">
        Open Replicant is an AI business built on an open source product. We
        believe infrastructure should tend itself — with people in the loop,
        holding the wheel, never out of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Our approach</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Open first</h3>
        <p>
          Morphogen is open source (Apache-2.0). Self-host it, inspect the
          knowledge kernel, extend it. No black boxes, no vendor lock-in. The
          kernel moves to its own repository once a second distribution needs
          it.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Governed AI</h3>
        <p>
          Model output is only ever a proposal. Six guarantees are enforced by
          the store and checked by a conformance suite — not left to
          convention. Every claim attributed, referenced, cited. Nothing deleted
          without a trace. Scope never widened. Clearance from people, never
          models. No method verifies its own output. Every answer shows its
          work.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Self-managing</h3>
        <p>
          Morphogen runs a MAPE-K loop: monitor, analyse, plan, approve, act,
          verify. It watches your systems, notices drift, and proposes governed
          changes you can review before they run.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Self-modifying</h3>
        <p>
          Gate G2: Morphogen can propose a better version of one of its own
          parts, build it, score it in a sandbox against the incumbent, and wait
          for your approval. Only when the observed result matches the
          prediction does it commit — changing itself through its own loop.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Services backed</h3>
        <p>
          Not everyone wants to self-host. Our consulting and implementation
          team helps you adopt Morphogen on your terms and timeline.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>SaaS roadmap</h3>
        <p>
          A hosted, managed offering is coming soon for teams that want
          Morphogen without operating it. Join the waitlist.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
